Third-party software
--------------------
backup-manager does not copy third-party code into its own source files. It
runs on Node.js with the libraries listed under "dependencies" in package.json
(Ink, React, Hono, commander, croner, node-tar, picomatch, zod and what they
depend on). npm installs them next to the program; the distribution packages
and the release tarball carry them under /usr/lib/backup-manager/node_modules
(bundle/node_modules in the tarball). Each library keeps its own licence (MIT,
ISC, BlueOak-1.0.0 or CC0-1.0, all compatible with the GPL version 3), and its
licence file is installed with it. The packages and the tarball also carry
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, which lists every library with its licence text.
